<title>USA: MBIA qualifies seven issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies seven issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following seven municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Flagstaff, Ariz., $17.5 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Boulder, Colo., $4.045 million certificates of participation, by direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Concord, N.H., $16.247 million GO capital improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Cheektowaga Union Free School District, N.Y., $6.6 million school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Royalton Central School District, N.Y., $5.057 million school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Shillington Borough, Pa., $2.965 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Waco, Texas, $8.490 million combined purpose bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
